From: Gaudi port <gaudi-port@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:25:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch 62: opt-in runtime expert mask (GLM53_EXPERT_MASK) for
 grouped-top-k routing on HPU

Per-layer [num_experts] additive mask buffer (0 kept / finfo.min dropped) installed after weight load by the FP8,
compressed-tensors and unquantized MoE methods and passed into vLLM's cpu_moe.select_experts (patch 63) so dropped
experts can never be selected; weights stay the survivors' unbiased sigmoid scores, renormalised. Zero effect when
unset. Fails loud if a MoE method never installed the attribute. CPU unit test in tests/unit_tests/ops.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
